<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Argyll and the Isles</h1><p class="st-meta">1156 CE – 1164 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short-lived sea realm of Somerled, who seized the southern Hebrides from the kings of Man and founded the dynasty of the Lords of the Isles.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerled">Somerled</a>, a Norse-Gaelic warlord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a> married to a daughter of Olaf I of Man, challenged his brother-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godred-olafsson">Godred</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-isles">Kingdom of the Isles</a>. After a sea battle in 1156 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> were divided, and in 1158 Somerled drove Godred from Man, ruling Argyll, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kintyre">Kintyre</a> and the southern isles.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerled">Somerled's</a> power rested on galley fleets and the loyalty of Gaelic and Norse-Gaelic kindreds. He acted as an independent ruler, sometimes allied with and sometimes against the Scottish king, and is linked with the founding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddell-abbey">Saddell Abbey</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kintyre">Kintyre</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerled">Somerled</a> was killed in 1164 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-renfrew">Renfrew</a> while invading the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-scotland">Kingdom of Scotland</a>. His realm was divided among his sons, ancestors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clan-macdougall">MacDougalls</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clan-donald">MacDonalds</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clann-ruaidhri">MacRuairis</a>, whose descendants later formed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-the-isles">Lordship of the Isles</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1156 CE – 1164 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.71%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1156 CE – 1164 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Somerled</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaelic, Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Realm of Somerled, Clann Somhairle lordship</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1160&amp;focus=kingdom-of-argyll-and-the-isles" aria-label="Kingdom of Argyll and the Isles on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4612 328 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Argyll and the Isles lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4897 579h0M5225 425h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4932 584h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4932 584h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United Kingdom. <a href="/atlas?year=1160&amp;focus=kingdom-of-argyll-and-the-isles">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
